# GMM-OT VC on LibriSpeech Short-Reference Pairs

This notebook tests a direct extension of MKL-VC: replace the single-Gaussian transport map with a per-dimension Gaussian-mixture transport map on the most target-variant WavLM dimensions.

The rest of the pipeline stays the same as kNN-VC/MKL-VC:

- WavLM encoder from official kNN-VC
- same LibriSpeech pair generation
- same HiFi-GAN vocoder
- same WER/CER/SIM evaluation

The key experimental question:

> Can a small 1D GMM transport preserve non-Gaussian target shapes, especially bimodal/heavy-tailed high-variance dimensions, better than MKL-VC's Gaussian map?

Default setting is a 200-pair pilot. Full 7800-pair runs are possible, but GMM fitting is much slower than MKL.

## 1. Runtime

In Colab, choose `Runtime > Change runtime type > GPU` before running.
