"""## 9. Notes

- `GMM_COMPONENTS = 1` is the sanity baseline: it collapses to per-dimension affine Gaussian transport.
- `GMM_COMPONENTS = 2` is the main hypothesis test for bimodal high-variance dimensions.
- `GMM_COMPONENTS = 3` may capture shoulders/heavy tails, but can overfit with one short target reference.
- `GMM_COMPONENT_MODE = 'target_bic'` selects K=1/2/3 per dimension using target-distribution BIC, then fits the source with the same K for ordered component matching.
- `GMM_MIN_SEPARATION_STD` is the guardrail: if fitted mixture components overlap too much, that dimension falls back to simple affine transport.
- `PRECOMPUTED_TOP_VARIANCE_DIMS` or `PRECOMPUTED_TOP_VARIANCE_DIMS_CSV` lets you use the same pooled high-variance dimensions from the Gaussianity/KDE notebooks, instead of noisy per-reference top dimensions.
- Low-variance dimensions are transported with one vectorized affine operation, so only the selected top dimensions pay the GMM fitting cost.
- Use the 200-pair pilot first. For full 7800 pairs, expect much longer runtime because every conversion fits many 1D GMMs.
- PESQ/STOI, if enabled, are proxy diagnostics against the source waveform, not primary non-parallel VC metrics.

"""

